```
Detection: Repeated failed authentication (brute force)
MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 - Brute Force
Data source: Windows Security Event Log (index=winlogs)

Logic: 5+ Event ID 4625 (failed logon) from the same source IP against the
same or different accounts within a 5-minute window.
```

index=winlogs EventCode=4625
| bin _time span=5m
| stats count as failed_attempts values(Account_Name) as targeted_accounts by src_ip, _time
| where failed_attempts >= 5

```
False positives:
- Service accounts with expired passwords retrying on a schedule
- A user who genuinely forgot their password and fat-fingered it a few times

Analyst triage:
1. Check if targeted_accounts is a single account (password spray suspicion if
   it's many accounts from one src_ip instead)
2. Cross-reference src_ip against known VPN/office egress IPs
3. If external/unrecognized src_ip: escalate as probable brute-force attempt
4. If internal + single account + <10 attempts: likely user error, note and close
```
